{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And the sense of ledashno.</b> To remove the ash from it. And the word ידשנה סלה (Psalms 20:4) means He will make from it ash, and the sense is that it be burned upon the altar and accepted; and behold תדשן עצם (Proverbs 15:30) is from a different binyan, namely the fat that is dense, and it is from the derivation of אשר שמנה לחמו (Genesis 49:20)." "<b>Ve'ayav.</b> Like ויעה ברד (Isaiah 28:17)." "<b>And the lamed of lekhol kelayv.</b> Added, like למן היום אשר יוסד בית ה' (Haggai 2:18)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra addresses an unusual word form in the verse; the exact form transliterated here reflects the Hebrew as given."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:40.892414374Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}